{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"godot gl tf 2.0 import workflow godot gl tf 2.0 import workflow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","fileName":"Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:18\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Open-Source Game Engine Asset Pipelines]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Open-Source Game Engine Asset Pipelines","Godot Imported Scene Instancing","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"godot gl tf 2.0 import workflow godot gl tf 2.0 import workflow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","fileName":"Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow","heading":"Godot glTF 2.0 Import Workflow","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The book recommends glTF 2.0 for moving its Blender environment into Godot because the format can preserve a useful real-time scene subset and is designed for efficient loading. The binary GLB form can package textures with the asset.\n\nOBJ lacks pivots and skeletal features, FBX is proprietary, and older COLLADA support can introduce compatibility limits. After import, the artist should inspect materials, hierarchy, transforms, and scale before [[Godot Imported Scene Instancing|instancing the scene]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Open-Source Game Engine Asset Pipelines","Godot Imported Scene Instancing","cre